    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        165.79172411764708,
        544.4649780285035,
        132.86440361344538,
        15.735210807600936
      ],
      "text": "Conclusion",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/RRZBDG+CMBX12",
        "size": 14.34619998931885
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        124.03413886554623,
        586.6096425178148,
        777.1832262605042,
        13.28006799287408
      ],
      "text": "In this article, we have shown that, when propensity scores are correctly specified, a particular",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/SHFDQT+CMR10",
        "size": 10.90909957885742
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        124.03413886554623,
        613.3426650831354,
        777.1650346638656,
        13.280067992874137
      ],
      "text": "restriction between the propensity score CDFs of treated and control groups must hold. Based",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/SHFDQT+CMR10",
        "size": 10.90909957885742
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        124.03413886554623,
        640.0756998218527,
        777.5412527310925,
        13.280067992874137
      ],
      "text": "on such restriction, we propose new nonparametric projection-based tests for the correct specifi-",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/SHFDQT+CMR10",
        "size": 10.90909957885742
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        124.03413886554623,
        666.662166864608,
        776.9577951680673,
        13.28006799287408
      ],
      "text": "cation of the propensity score. In contrast to other proposals, our tests are not severely affected",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/SHFDQT+CMR10",
        "size": 10.90909957885742
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        124.03413886554623,
        693.3952016033254,
        777.371430042017,
        13.280055819477411
      ],
      "text": "by the \u201ccurse of dimensionality\u201d\u2019, are not sensitive to the different estimation methods used to",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/SHFDQT+CMR10",
        "size": 10.90909957885742
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        124.03413886554623,
        720.127737232779,
        777.2229686974791,
        13.280092339667476
      ],
      "text": "estimate the propensity score under the null, do not rely on the potentially ad hoc choice of",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/SHFDQT+CMR10",
        "size": 10.90909957885742
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        124.03413886554623,
        746.7146790380048,
        776.9385527310925,
        13.28008016627075
      ],
      "text": "bandwidths, and enjoy some optimal power properties against particular classes of alternative",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/SHFDQT+CMR10",
        "size": 10.90909957885742
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        124.03413886554623,
        773.4472024940617,
        777.1653447478992,
        13.280080166270835
      ],
      "text": "hypotheses. We have derived the asymptotic properties of the proposed tests, and have proved",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/SHFDQT+CMR10",
        "size": 10.90909957885742
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        124.03413886554623,
        800.1802372327791,
        777.373325,
        13.280080166270778
      ],
      "text": "that they are able to detect local alternatives converging to the null at the parametric rate, and",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/SHFDQT+CMR10",
        "size": 10.90909957885742
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        124.03413886554623,
        826.766679928741,
        777.5999102941176,
        13.280092339667448
      ],
      "text": "that critical values can be easily computed via a simple multiplier bootstrap procedure. Our",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/SHFDQT+CMR10",
        "size": 10.90909957885742
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        124.03413886554623,
        853.4997146674584,
        777.3330657563025,
        13.280080166270807
      ],
      "text": "Monte Carlo simulation study illustrates that, for a large class of alternatives, our projection-",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/SHFDQT+CMR10",
        "size": 10.90909957885742
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        124.03413886554623,
        880.2322502969121,
        777.2394720588237,
        13.280080166270778
      ],
      "text": "based tests perform better in finite samples than existing tests, though there are some classes",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/SHFDQT+CMR10",
        "size": 10.90909957885742
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        124.03413886554623,
        906.8191957541568,
        777.352618277311,
        13.280074079572458
      ],
      "text": "of alternatives in which our tests have trivial power. All these finite sample findings are in line",
      "font": {
        "color": [
          0,
          0,
          0,
          255
        ],
        "name": "/SHFDQT+CMR10",
        "size": 10.90909957885742
      }
    },
    {
      "bbox": [
        503.36992016806727,
        963.7906909738717,
        18.69908361344534,
        13.280080166270785
      ],
      "text": "29",
